{%- doc -%}
  Renders the unit price, including its measurement — e.g. "£120/l".

  Reconstructed from wb-money + the measurement (rather than the
  `unit_price_with_measurement` filter) so the amount is tidied server-side (drop
  .00) exactly like the main price, with no currency code (the main price carries
  it) and no client-side flash on variant/cart re-render. Matches the unit price in
  snippets/product-tagline.liquid — keep the two in step. Note: this uses the raw
  reference_unit ("l"), so it reads "/l" not the filter's "/L".

  @param {number} price - The unit price in cents.
  @param {object} measurement - The unit_price_measurement object.
  @param {boolean} [hide_accessibility_label] - Whether to hide the accessibility label (default: false).

  @example
  {% render 'unit-price', price: variant.unit_price, measurement: variant.unit_price_measurement %}
{%- enddoc -%}
<small class="unit-price caption">
  {%- unless hide_accessibility_label -%}
    <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'products.product.price.unit_price' | t }}</span>
  {%- endunless -%}
  <span class="wb-product-price price-item price-item--last">
    {%- render 'wb-money', amount: price, code: false -%}
    {%- if measurement -%}/{%- if measurement.reference_value != 1 -%}{{ measurement.reference_value }}{%- endif -%}{{ measurement.reference_unit }}{%- endif -%}
  </span>
</small>
